Register GDAL's drivers in the extensions that open datasets.

This removes one of two known iOS blockers; it is NOT established that it makes
fiona writes work. `tests/test_fiona.py::test_write_read_geojson` skips on iOS
with a different diagnosis — that OGR's GeoJSON writer calls into PROJ to stamp
a default WGS84 field, fails with `Cannot find proj.db`, and surfaces as the
same `FionaNullPointerError`. Both explanations are supported: the missing
`proj.db` is confirmed (gdal's own example raised
`proj_create_from_database: Cannot find proj.db` on an iPhone 16 simulator on
2026-08-25), and the registry split below is confirmed by call sites. Whichever
fires first, this patch fixes the registry half and nothing else. Do not remove
that skip on the strength of this patch — remove it when a device run passes.

Third package with the same defect, after rasterio and pyogrio, and the same
cause: `flet-libgdal` ships only `libgdal.a` on iOS, so each extension links
its own copy of GDAL and each copy carries its own driver registry.

fiona registers in `_env`. But `ogrext` — where `fiona.open` actually does its
work — opens datasets in a registry nothing populates. Call sites on iOS
arm64, counted with `otool -tV` because every extension *defines* the symbols
and `nm` therefore cannot tell you who calls them:

    _env        GDALAllRegister x1, OGRRegisterAll x1, GDALOpenEx x123
    ogrext      GDALOpenEx x117, GDALGetDriverByName x45, no registration
    _geometry   GDALOpenEx x115, no registration
    _transform  GDALOpenEx x115, no registration

The measured symptom is consistent with this: `fiona._env` reports a driver
registry identical to Android's — because that is `_env`'s own — while every
write fails in `fiona.ogrext` with `FionaNullPointerError: NULL pointer error`.
Consistent with, not proof of; see the caveat above.

`crs.pyx` is deliberately not patched: it does not `include "gdal.pxi"`, and
its lookups are OSR/CRS work rather than dataset opens.

`GDALAllRegister()` and `OGRRegisterAll()` are idempotent, so on Android — one
shared `libgdal.so`, one registry — this changes nothing.

Same limit as the rasterio and pyogrio patches: the copies remain separate GDAL
instances, so configuration set through `fiona.Env()` still does not reach
`ogrext`. A shared libgdal for iOS is the complete fix and would retire all
three patches at once.

